From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 18:15:02 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 76/97] Plutonium: a touchpad swipe's begin and end keep their
 finger count

ScrollEvent's copy from a native event read the offsets of a fling cancel or
start but not its finger count, so a three-finger swipe's begin and end reached
Ash with none and never got to the shell (patch 0074): the shell library had to
guess the end from a pause in the updates.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ui/events/event.cc | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ui/events/event.cc b/ui/events/event.cc
index 20b5f8b72d..ba0cfa736b 100644
--- a/ui/events/event.cc
+++ b/ui/events/event.cc
@@ -1211,6 +1211,11 @@ ScrollEvent::ScrollEvent(const PlatformEvent& native_event)
              type() == EventType::kScrollFlingCancel) {
     GetFlingData(native_event, &x_offset_, &y_offset_, &x_offset_ordinal_,
                  &y_offset_ordinal_, nullptr);
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_OZONE)
+    // PLUTONIUM: a touchpad swipe's begin and end (a fling cancel and start)
+    // keep their finger count, so Ash can hand them to the shell.
+    finger_count_ = native_event->AsScrollEvent()->finger_count();
+#endif
   } else {
     NOTREACHED() << "Unexpected event type " << std::to_underlying(type())
                  << " when constructing a ScrollEvent.";
